  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "WEG CFW500 drives as a Modbus RTU slave on the RS-485 port of the plug-in module (Modbus RTU User's Guide 10002253377 rev 04); parameter scaling from the V2.2X programming manual.",
  "summary": "WEG's general-purpose variable frequency drive. Over Modbus RTU every drive parameter is a 16-bit holding register whose address equals the parameter number, so P0680 status word is register 680 and P0682/P0683 control word and speed reference are 682/683. This map covers the read-only monitoring parameters, the status/control words, the command-source and serial-port setup parameters, and the network-driven digital/analog outputs.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The Modbus guide says parameters are mapped with offset zero: the parameter number is the holding register address (P0100 = address 100 = 0064h), and it lists P0680 at holding register address 680. So P0680 is requested as address 680; a master that numbers holding registers from 40001 needs 40681. Values travel as plain integers with no decimal point; the guide says the number of decimal places comes from the programming manual, so scale here follows the decimals in each parameter's range there (e.g. P0003 0.0-200.0 A -> 0.1 A)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "Programming manual for software V2.2X (doc 10002296099 rev 07); Modbus guide rev 04 adds STO/Fire Mode status bits and PID control bits",
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus RTU CFW500 User's Guide",
    "doc_number": "10002253377 / 04",
    "revision_date": "2025-06",
    "url": "https://static.weg.net/medias/downloadcenter/h73/ha4/WEG-CFW500-modbus-rtu-manual-10002253377-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Modbus guide: parameters ch. 4 printed pp. 4-1 to 4-13 (P0220-P0228, P0308-P0316, P0680-P0683, P0695-P0698), memory map and function codes ch. 5 pp. 5-1 to 5-2. Programming manual V2.2X: quick reference pp. 0-1 to 0-26, status/control words section 7.3 pp. 7-13 to 7-16, reading parameters ch. 18 pp. 18-1 to 18-6, fault history 17-8 to 17-10."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Scaling and the P0001-P0070 monitoring parameters come from the WEG CFW500 Programming Manual V2.2X, doc 10002296099 rev 07 (09/2024), https://static.weg.net/medias/downloadcenter/h69/h0f/WEG-CFW500-programming-manual-10002296099-en.pdf. Newer firmware (V3.x/V4.x) manuals were not available in English from WEG's server, so check P0023 on site; parameter numbers for these core points are the same in the R04 Modbus guide.",
    "P0001 and P0002 are left unscaled: they use the user scale from P0208 (full-scale value), P0209 (unit) and P0210 (decimal point). With the factory defaults the scale is Hz with one decimal.",
    "P0681 and P0683 use WEG's 13-bit scale: 8192 equals the motor rated frequency P0403, so Hz = value x P0403 / 8192, saturating at +/-32767 (4x rated).",
    "Left out: P0040/P0041 PID process variable and setpoint (decimal places depend on P0529), fault-history currents/voltages for the second and third faults (P0061-P0074, same format as P0051-P0055), and P0684/P0685 (fieldbus-card control word and reference, not used over the serial port).",
    "The R04 Modbus guide shows P0680 bit 0 as STO and bit 2 as Fire Mode, and P0682 bits 13/14 as internal/external PID manual select; the V2.2X programming manual marks those bits reserved. Older firmware will leave them at 0.",
    "The Modbus guide lists P0308 as 0-255; the programming manual lists 1-247. Use 1-247.",
    "Fault and alarm numbers are the F/A codes without the letter (P0049 = 228 means F0228 serial timeout).",
    "P0312 options 1, 3, 8, 9, 14 and 15 (SymbiNet and BACnet) come from the R04 Modbus guide; the V2.2X programming manual lists them as Reserved, so they need newer firmware."
  ],
