  "integration": {
    "summary": "Leave P0312 = 2 (Modbus RTU on the standard RS-485), match P0308/P0310/P0311 to the master, then point the remote command sources at Serial/USB (P0220, P0222 = 9, P0226, P0227 = 2). Write the P0682 control word (e.g. 0x0017 = run + general enable + forward + remote; 0x0016 = ramp stop) and P0683 in the 8192 = rated-frequency scale, and poll P0680, P0005, P0003 and P0049.",
    "minimum_registers": [
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 682,
        "why": "Control word: run, enable, direction, fault reset"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 683,
        "why": "Speed reference, 8192 = P0403"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 680,
        "why": "Status word: running, remote, fault"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 5,
        "why": "Output frequency (0.1 Hz)"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 3,
        "why": "Motor current (0.1 A)"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 4,
        "why": "DC link voltage"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 49,
        "why": "Present fault number"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 48,
        "why": "Present alarm number"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "P0312 selects the serial protocol (2 = Modbus RTU slave on serial 1, 7 = on the second port of a CRS485/CUSB/CRS232 module). Set P0308 address, P0310 baud and P0311 byte format. For network control set P0220 = 1 (always Remote) or 6 (Local/Remote switched by P0682 bit 4), P0222 = 9 (reference from P0683), P0226 = 5 or 6 (direction from P0682 bit 2) and P0227 = 2 (run/stop from P0682). Use P0221/P0223/P0224 instead if the drive runs in Local.",
    "watchdog": "P0314 Serial Watchdog (0.0-999.0 s, 0 = off by default) raises alarm A0128 when no valid telegram arrives in time; P0313 picks the reaction (0 none, 1 ramp stop default, 2 coast/general disable, 3 go to Local, 4 Local keeping the network commands, 5 fault F0228). Timing starts at the first valid telegram after power-up. P0316 shows 2 while the watchdog error is active.",
    "quirks": [
      "Register address = parameter number, no offset: P0680 is address 680 (40681 in 4x-style masters).",
      "Everything is a 16-bit integer with the decimal point dropped; check the programming manual for each parameter's decimals.",
      "P0683 speed reference is not in Hz: 8192 = motor rated frequency (P0403). For 30 Hz on a 60 Hz motor write 4096.",
      "Negative P0683 reverses the reference, and P0682 bit 2 also flips direction; both together cancel out.",
      "P0682 and P0683 show as read-only on the keypad but are writable over the network.",
      "Supported functions: 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 06, 15, 16 and 43 (device identification)."
    ],
    "setup": [
      "RS-485 on the plug-in module terminals: the standard CFW500-IOS module carries A(-), B(+) and GND; check the terminal label of the fitted module (the Modbus guide and programming manual print different terminal numbers).",
      "Baud 9600, 19200 (default) or 38400; byte format 8N1, 8E1 (default), 8O1, 8N2, 8E2 or 8O2.",
      "Fit 120 ohm termination only at the two ends of the trunk; up to 32 devices per segment, 1000 m max.",
      "P0027 shows which plug-in module the drive detected.",
      "Most command-source parameters (P0220-P0228, P0312) are 'cfg' and can only be changed with the motor stopped."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "If a password is set in P0200, parameter writes are refused until the password is written to P0000; access resets at power-down.",
      "P0220 factory setting is 2 (HMI key, starting in Local), so network run commands are ignored until Remote is selected.",
      "Factory P0227 = 1 (digital inputs): network run/stop is ignored until it is set to 2.",
      "When the drive uses the RS-485 port for a remote keypad (P0312 = 0), Modbus is off on that port; use a two-port module and P0312 = 6 for keypad plus Modbus.",
      "With P0229 = 1 (coast stop), P0682 bit 0 behaves like bit 1 and the motor coasts."
    ]
  },
  "verified": {
    "date": "2026-10-25",
    "method": "independent re-check of every register against the source PDF",
    "pages": "Modbus guide 10002253377 R04: pp. 4-1 to 4-13 (P0220-P0228, P0308-P0316, P0680-P0683, P0695-P0698), 5-1 to 5-2 (functions, offset-zero memory map, 'data is transmitted as an integer value' decimals rule), 6-1, 7-1. Programming manual 10002296099 R07 V2.2X: quick reference 0-1 to 0-12, 5-2 (password), 7-14 to 7-16 (P0680/P0690/P0682/P0229), 17-8 to 17-10 (fault history), 18-1 to 18-5, 19-1 to 19-3",
